spec:
  grid: 16x16, bg=7
  cutouts:
    count: 2 tailed black(0) cutouts
    core: 3x4 or 4x3 solid rectangle (area=12)
    tail: 2 cells extending from the middle of one side (middle row for 3-row core, middle col for 3-col core)
    tail_direction: any of top/bottom/left/right relative to core
    total_cells: 14
  staircases:
    count: exactly 1 active gray(5) source + exactly 1 non-gray colored distractor staircase
    shape: right-triangle staircase, each row 1 cell shorter than the row above; top edge and one lateral edge fully filled
    height: 3-5 rows, width: 3-8 cols (width >= height)
    border: each staircase touches exactly one grid edge; hypotenuse faces grid interior
  distractors:
    single_pixels: 1-2 colored single-pixel cells; unique colors per role
    extra_black: 0-1 additional black objects (single pixel or small <=2x2 rectangle) [observed]
  selection_rule: |
    For each tailed cutout, cast horizontal rays LEFT and RIGHT from each core row through bg.
    A ray hitting a non-bg cell counts only if it is a gray source pixel; any
    non-gray colored region or black object blocks the ray as a distractor.
    The unique (cutout, side) pair with the max gray-source hit count wins.
  transform: erase the winning cutout's tail to bg; paint the winning side column of its core pink(6)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Place the active gray(5) staircase source touching one border, choosing height and row band.
    2. Build the winning cutout core (3x4 or 4x3) positioned so the source-facing side has clear horizontal LOS to the staircase for >=2 core rows (more rows than any other cutout-side pair will get).
    3. Add a 2-cell tail to the winning cutout on any side of the core (from the middle row/col).
    4. Place the second tailed cutout elsewhere, ensuring it gets strictly fewer source hits on every side.
    5. Add exactly one non-gray staircase distractor on either border; it may block rays but never counts as a source.
    6. Optionally add same-color single-pixel markers for distractor colors.
    7. Scatter 1-2 standalone single-pixel distractors; optionally add extra small black objects.
    8. Verify uniqueness: the winning (cutout, side) pair has strictly the most hits. Reject otherwise.
```
